        "note": "Still open against the accepted rationale. The tests now call input-parameterized methods with multiple values and restrict lexical construct checks to each method, but they still accept hard-coded branches for every public input plus the required %, switch/->, and for tokens inside `if (false)` dead branches. On Temurin 25.0.4.1 and Maven 3.9.11, that adversarial program passed all 6 public tests. The original finding explicitly identified hard-coded results and dead branches, so the current lexical checks do not substantiate the README claim."
